{"title":"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the smallest positive number from the numbers below.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96fddc1e2834d11082a880b26a32e818c9cf2115.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\ 10-3\\sqrt{11} \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)} \\ 3\\sqrt{11}-10 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)}\\ 18-5\\sqrt{13}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 51-10\\sqrt{26}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 10\\sqrt{26}-51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"735\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a03efc7a40f1fd2c39074bfbc234a47d8a1bd8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\sqrt{11} - 10 = \\sqrt{99} - \\sqrt{100} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"238\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/74360b2aee9af5874830f420cca56ea8d272d16d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 - 5\\sqrt{13} = \\sqrt{324} - \\sqrt{325} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"247\" height=\"18\" />, and similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/459c8434679c08d628c97ad8a7668e97c6a97a0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\sqrt{26} - 51 = \\sqrt{2600} - \\sqrt{2601} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"274\" height=\"18\" />, so these numbers can be excluded immediately as they are negative and we seek the smallest <b>positive</b> number. The remaining choices are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/3/5c38e7ae76e4e05519f9a03fbd5986f6fb2c8b62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 - 3\\sqrt{11} = \\sqrt{100} - \\sqrt{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/c/14c2c763f76be32f72995b51b48305bc85b1bbf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51 - 10\\sqrt{26} = \\sqrt{2601} - \\sqrt{2600}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" />. Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/9/bc936843a4f68765f24c2a2ed03e0d823b48d75f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{100} - \\sqrt{99} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{100} + \\sqrt{99}} \\approx \\frac{1}{10+10} = \\frac{1}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"355\" height=\"41\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52bfc2dc1a382b61259463ec92b77c3634fe008f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2601} - \\sqrt{2600} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2601} + \\sqrt{2600}} \\approx \\frac{1}{51+51} = \\frac{1}{102} &lt; \\frac{1}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"466\" height=\"41\" />, so the smallest positive number in the list is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db501a49566e8d4f0ff3c9d85195e0a43f87774d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\ 51 - 10 \\sqrt{26}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"138\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After reaching the two possibilities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/f/8bf64ef59124f3c73048da0866fadc9b3aed2cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{100}-\\sqrt{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc16f182e19c7a459e0e131fc170dae9f0bc83a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2601}-\\sqrt{2600}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> as in the first solution, note that these can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d17c5122666592fbf53e78156ac6438db90e450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"19\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d8f8e9675091b6c67807f22cedce7360d82b43f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a781491fb8b749a347e34802c09673103e4f19fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2601$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fb2eb3a43300997e25d3f60eee8145ddeeb7f2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{x-1}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} - \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x-1}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{x-1} - \\sqrt{x}}{2\\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{x-1}} &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"474\" height=\"45\" /> (as the numerator is always negative and the denominator is always positive for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791aa0ff911a09ac656cd5ce7638ca8e64805d8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />). Therefore, with its derivative being negative, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d17c5122666592fbf53e78156ac6438db90e450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"19\" /> is a strictly decreasing function over its domain, so the smaller value will be the one with the larger value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c45c15874770db37f4e422040684a3b51d097c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2601$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db501a49566e8d4f0ff3c9d85195e0a43f87774d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\ 51 - 10 \\sqrt{26}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"138\" height=\"33\" /> as before.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>